Source: crete
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ashwin Balaji <s.ashwinbalaji.de@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 12), g++, make, pkg-config,
 nasm [amd64 i386], gawk, libsdl2-dev, libgl-dev
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://codeberg.org/abksh/Crete
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: crete
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: dynamic-range and loudness meter (TT DR, EBU R128, true peak)
 crete measures TT Dynamic Range (the dr.loudness-war.info PMF procedure),
 EBU R128 integrated loudness and loudness range, true peak (4x
 oversampled), PLR/PSR and crest factor, per channel and for stereo, quad,
 5.1 and 7.1.
 .
 This build includes the compact FFmpeg decoder set (ALAC, AAC, MP3, Opus,
 Vorbis, WMA, WavPack, APE, Musepack, TAK, Dolby TrueHD/AC-3/E-AC-3, DTS
 and DTS-HD MA) alongside the native WAV/RF64/AIFF/FLAC/DSF/DFF/SACD ISO
 readers.

Package: crete-gui
Architecture: any
Depends: crete (= ${binary:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: zenity | kdialog
Description: graphical front-end for the crete dynamic-range meter
 Dear ImGui / SDL2 front-end for crete: the same measurement engine as the
 command-line tool, with per-channel meters, album tables and stream
 selection for multi-stream disc rips.
